55}}, {"n": 25, "w": "exactly", "pos": "adv.", "zh": "正是；完全对", "ex": "Exactly means correct in every way. People also say Exactly! to agree strongly.", "exs": ["Exactly! That's what I mean.", "It costs exactly fifty dollars."], "t": 629.88, "src": {"t": "Yeah exactly, so it’s better that it’s earned fame.", "a": "audio/t08/s13.mp3", "hl": [5, 12], "sp": "Naval", "oa": "audio/t08o/s13.mp3", "oab": [0.06, 2.91]}, "tt": {"w": 629.88, "ex": [["Exactly", 633.0], ["means", 633.0], ["correct", 633.52], ["in", 633.9], ["every", 634.22], ["way.", 634.48], ["People", 634.84], ["also", 635.48], ["say", 635.98], ["Exactly!", 636.3], ["to", 637.12], ["agree", 637.48], ["strongly.", 637.74]], "exs": [[["Exactly!", 641.6], ["That's", 641.64], ["what", 642.38], ["I", 642.5], ["mean.", 642.62]], [["It", 646.86], ["costs", 647.03], ["exactly", 647.08], ["fifty", 647.48], ["dollars.", 648.04]]], "z": [643.56, 649.22], "o": 651.77}}, {"n": 26, "w": "tribe", "pos": "n.", "zh": "部落；（有共同点的）群体", "ex": "A tribe is a group of people who live together and share the same culture. Today it can mean your group or community.", "exs": ["My lash community feels like a tribe.", "Early humans lived in tribes."], "t": 656.12, "src": {"t": "For example, earned respect in the tribe is you do things that are good for the tribe.", "a": "audio/t08/s14.mp3", "hl": [35, 40], "sp": "Naval", "oa": "audio/t08o/s14.mp3", "oab": [0, 2.3]}, "tt": {"w": 656.12, "ex": [["A", 659.05], ["tribe", 659.16], ["is", 659.5], ["a", 659.67], ["group", 659.78], ["of", 660.12], ["people", 660.29], ["who", 660.29], ["live", 660.29], ["together", 660.54], ["and", 661.1], ["share", 661.66], ["the", 662.22], ["same", 662.78], ["culture.", 663.34], ["Today", 663.9], ["it", 664.46], ["can", 665.02], ["mean", 665.58], ["your", 665.58], ["group", 665.58], ["or", 665.58], ["community.", 665.58]], "exs": [[["My", 668.92], ["lash", 668.94], ["community", 669.5], ["feels", 670.06], ["like", 670.62], ["a", 671.18], ["tribe.", 671.23]], [["Early", 675.7], ["humans", 676.26], ["lived", 676.82], ["in", 677.38], ["tribes.", 677.43]]], "z": [671.8, 678.0], "o": 681.12}}, {"n": 27, "w": "transcend", "pos": "v.", "zh": "超越", "ex": "To transcend means to go beyond the normal limits of something. To transcend the self means to think beyond only yourself.", "exs": ["Great music transcends language.", "Some people transcend their ego."], "t": 684.77, "src": {"t": "Who are the most famous people in human history? There are people who sort of transcended the self, the Buddhas and the Jesuses and the Mohammads of the world.", "a": "audio/t08/s15.mp3", "hl": [78, 89], "sp": "Naval", "oa": "audio/t08o/s15.mp3", "oab": [5.88, 7.84]}, "tt": {"w": 684.77, "ex": [["To", 687.93], ["transcend", 688.12], ["means", 688.74], ["to", 689.11], ["go", 689.3], ["beyond", 689.3], ["the", 689.3], ["normal", 689.34], ["limits", 689.9], ["of", 690.46], ["something.", 691.02], ["To", 691.58], ["transcend", 692.14], ["the", 692.52], ["self", 692.98], ["means", 693.26], ["to", 693.55], ["think", 693.83], ["beyond", 694.12], ["only", 694.67], ["yourself.", 695.22]], "exs": [[["Great", 698.8], ["music", 698.82], ["transcends", 699.26], ["language.", 699.92]], [["Some", 704.53], ["people", 704.57], ["transcend", 704.93], ["their", 705.31], ["ego.", 705.85]]], "z": [701.2, 706.91], "o": 709.57}}, {"n": 28, "w": "discover", "pos": "v.", "zh": "发现", "ex": "To discover means to find something for the first time, something nobody knew before.", "exs": ["Scientists discover new things every day.", "I discovered a great lash supplier."], "t": 712.87, "src": {"t": "Who else is famous? The artists are famous—art lasts for a long time. The scientists are famous—they discover things.", "a": "audio/t08/s16.mp3", "hl": [101, 109], "sp": "Naval", "oa": "audio/t08o/s16.mp3", "oab": [4.56, 6.48]}, "tt": {"w": 712.87, "ex": [["To", 715.75], ["discover", 715.92], ["means", 716.42], ["to", 716.76], ["find", 716.92], ["something", 717.2], ["for", 717.76], ["th